WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.840
Health-CUA asks whether AI agents can do real clinical work inside an electronic health record.

2
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:14.700
Each agent gets the same task on the same patient record, through the API, our screens, or OpenMRS.

3
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:22.041
On screen, the agent works like a person. It reads the chart, clicks, types, and signs the order.

4
00:00:22.741 --> 00:00:26.621
OpenMRS is an open source record system that we did not build.

5
00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:31.761
We tested fifteen models on thirty nine real specialist consultations.

6
00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:36.981
The strongest models complete about as many tasks on screen as through the API.

7
00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:48.641
Memory decides success on screen. With only its last three screenshots, Claude Sonnet 5.5 solves one percent of tasks. With its full history, sixty nine percent.

8
00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:54.982
In OpenMRS, the same agents complete fifteen to nineteen points fewer tasks.

9
00:00:55.682 --> 00:01:01.402
We also tested the grader, with scripts that order correctly, leave orders out, or order everything.

10
00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:07.142
Health-CUA. The leaderboard, the paper and the code are on the project page.
